      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I  represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram II  represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is also a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130099/assets/23a5a5e1a1ddf23caaadbbc3645694c8b21f8ec111149a1193d08b958dd659d7.svg)  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
